      "body": "**Description:**\nIn `vllm/model_executor/warmup/deep_gemm_warmup.py`, the function `_fp8_linear_may_use_deep_gemm()` was unconditionally calling `get_mk_alignment_for_contiguous_layout()` before verifying if the module was actually an FP8 module. \n\nSince `get_mk_alignment_for_contiguous_layout()` throws a `RuntimeError` when the DeepGEMM backend is missing or outdated (e.g., on non-Hopper hardware), this caused vLLM to instantly crash during model warmup for **all** models (including standard `bfloat16` models like Qwen2.5-VL), even though they never intended to use DeepGEMM.\n\n**Fix:**\nMoved the `block_size = get_mk_alignment_for_contiguous_layout()[0]` execution strictly below the module type-checking guard. This ensures the alignment check (and potential `RuntimeError`) is only ever evaluated if the module is definitively confirmed to be an FP8 linear module.\n",
      "changedFiles": 1,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
