            "body": "## Code Review\n\nThis pull request modifies the `_fp8_linear_may_use_deep_gemm` function to add a check for `quant_method` and delay the `block_size` calculation. The reviewer pointed out that the new check is redundant and recommended verifying if DeepGEMM is enabled to ensure compatibility with older NVIDIA GPUs.",
            "comments": {
              "nodes": [
                {
                  "author": {
                    "__typename": "Bot",
                    "login": "gemini-code-assist"
                  },
                  "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nThe addition of `getattr(module, \"quant_method\", None) is not None` is redundant because the preceding `isinstance(module, LinearBase)` check already guarantees that the `quant_method` attribute exists on the module.\n\nMore importantly, to fully resolve the risk of a `RuntimeError` on unsupported hardware (e.g., NVIDIA GPUs older than Hopper) for FP8 models, the guard should explicitly verify if DeepGEMM is enabled and supported for this specific module. By checking `getattr(module.quant_method, \"use_deep_gemm\", False)`, you ensure that `get_mk_alignment_for_contiguous_layout()` is only invoked when the DeepGEMM backend is actually available and intended for use. This makes the fix robust for FP8 models running on non-Hopper hardware.\n\n```suggestion\n        and isinstance(module.quant_method, Fp8LinearMethod)\n        and getattr(module.quant_method, \"use_deep_gemm\", False)\n```",
                  "createdAt": "2026-05-09T06:31:20Z",
                  "databaseId": 3212632528,
                  "diffHunk": "@@ -133,15 +133,17 @@ def _fp8_linear_may_use_deep_gemm(module: torch.nn.Module) -> bool:\n \n     # FIXME: this logic is brittle and incorrect - since we\n     # could use DeepGEMM with for than just Fp8LinearMethod\n-    block_size = get_mk_alignment_for_contiguous_layout()[0]\n+    \n     if not (\n         isinstance(module, LinearBase)\n+        and getattr(module, \"quant_method\", None) is not None\n         and isinstance(module.quant_method, Fp8LinearMethod)",
